/**
 * The HTTP endpoint the Self.xyz mobile app posts a proof to.
 *
 * This lived in the CLI, where it served exactly one caller: `buy verify serve`
 * spins up a tunnel, holds ONE pending `VerificationRequest`, and waits for ONE
 * proof to arrive. That shape is why the client needs `cloudflared` at all — the
 * party that wants the attestation is made to run a public web server.
 *
 * Moving it here is what lets a GATEWAY host the same endpoint instead, and the
 * move forces two changes the single-session version did not need:
 *
 *   - `request` is resolved PER REQUEST rather than read from one variable. A
 *     server fields proofs from many callers it has never heard of, and has to
 *     decide what each one should be checked against.
 *   - persistence is a callback rather than a keystore write. The CLI stores an
 *     attestation for its own account; a server stores it for whoever proved it,
 *     somewhere durable and shared.
 *
 * It lives in `@celo/buy-identity` and not in `@celo/buy` because `@celo/buy`
 * publishes a `bin` and no `main` or `exports` — nothing can import from it.
 */
